Diagnostic-only supplement to kexec_secure_sp_tz_reclaim_diag_6.6.89.patch.

Apply directly to the base helper C SHA256
b99466b05dfc4b360533688b8d442239dcb65c122bffc97f60b8eb126ac45dda;
do not combine with the SCM tracing supplement for this isolation test.

preserve_for_skip_diag defaults to false and is read-only (0400). Explicit true
still requires the original armed, identity, live-DT, offline-seal, device/rproc
locks and exact empty-pool checks. Only after pool=NULL does it bypass SCM and
the SCM-specific owners==HLOS postcondition, then release the original locks.
It neither reads/writes backing RAM nor changes firmware ownership. False keeps
the original SCM arguments, owner postcondition, identity checks and logging.

MANDATORY EXTERNAL PRECONDITION for explicit true: independently audit the
actual loaded target DT, not merely its input file, to confirm both secure-sp-tz
and secure-sp-modem heap consumers are disabled while their exact reserved
regions remain reserved/no-map and unreused. Also complete the normal exact
source/module/target identity and successful freeze/handoff preflight. This
module cannot inspect or verify the loaded target DT and does not arm itself.

This is a one-way, single-test mechanism isolation diagnostic, not ownership
proof or a final fix. It preserves only the existing SP-TZ isolation operation;
it never touches SP-modem. Seal/pool isolation are not rolled back and must not
return to Android; all original fail-closed/reset behavior remains. The caller
must use the verified nonreturning ARM64 kexec handoff and ordinary reset on any
later failure. A target with either heap enabled is outside this experiment.

--- a/secure_heap_reclaim.c
+++ b/secure_heap_reclaim.c
@@ -78,6 +78,9 @@
 static_assert(offsetof(struct rproc, recovery_disabled) == 0x4dc);
 static_assert(offsetof(struct rproc, auto_boot) == 0x509);
 
+static bool preserve_for_skip_diag;
+module_param(preserve_for_skip_diag, bool, 0400);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(preserve_for_skip_diag, "Preserve isolated SP-TZ ownership without SCM; requires external actual loaded-DT two-heap disable audit");
 static bool armed;
 module_param(armed, bool, 0400);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(armed, "Required one-use arm; consumed only by the exact frozen kexec restart notification");
@@ -263,6 +266,14 @@
 	pr_emerg("phase=isolated heap=%s base=%pa size=%#lx old_owners=%#llx dst=%u perms=%u\n",
 		 SHRC_HEAP, &ctx.sc->carveout.base, SHRC_SIZE, owners,
 		 SHRC_HLOS_VMID, SHRC_HLOS_RWX);
+	if (preserve_for_skip_diag) {
+		if (!shrc_rproc_offline() || !shrc_private_identity() ||
+		    READ_ONCE(ctx.sc->carveout.pool))
+			shrc_fatal("post-preserve-identity", -EINVAL);
+		pr_emerg("phase=preserved heap=%s base=%pa size=%#lx no_scm=1 owner_unchanged_by_helper=1 pool_present=0 continue_kexec=1 external_loaded_dtb_two_heap_disabled_required=1\n",
+			 SHRC_HEAP, &ctx.sc->carveout.base, SHRC_SIZE);
+		goto release_locks;
+	}
 	ret = qcom_scm_assign_mem(SHRC_BASE, SHRC_SIZE, &owners, &destination, 1);
 	if (ret || owners != BIT_ULL(SHRC_HLOS_VMID))
 		shrc_fatal("scm-reclaim", ret ?: -EIO);
@@ -271,6 +282,7 @@
 		shrc_fatal("post-reclaim-identity", -EINVAL);
 	pr_emerg("phase=reclaimed heap=%s owners_after=%#llx pool_present=0 continue_kexec=1\n",
 		 SHRC_HEAP, owners);
+release_locks:
 	up_write(&ctx.sc->carveout.mem_sem);
 	mutex_unlock(&ctx.rproc->lock);
 	device_unlock(ctx.heap_parent);
